---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getPublishedSoftware } from "@/data/software";

const products = getPublishedSoftware();
const effective = "31 August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — BramLabs"
  description="How BramLabs handles personal information on bramlabs.co. Individual products have their own policies, linked here."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="h-page">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="doc-meta effective">Effective {effective}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="summary">
          This policy covers the bramlabs.co website. Each product has its own
          policy covering what that product does — those are linked below and take
          precedence for the product they describe.
        </p>

        <h2>Who this is</h2>
        <p>
          BramLabs is an independent studio run by one person, publishing software
          and original design work. Contact:
          <a href="mailto:contact@bramlabs.co">contact@bramlabs.co</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What this website collects</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Category</th>
                <th scope="col">What</th>
                <th scope="col">Why</th>
                <th scope="col">Kept for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Form submissions</th>
                <td>
                  Whatever you type into the contact or feedback form — your
                  message, and your email address if you provide one.
                </td>
                <td>To reply to you and to fix what you reported.</td>
                <td>
                  While the matter is open, then up to 24 months. Deleted on
                  request.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Server logs</th>
                <td>
                  Standard request data recorded by the host: IP address,
                  timestamp, requested URL, and browser user agent.
                </td>
                <td>To keep the site up and to investigate abuse or errors.</td>
                <td>Held by Cloudflare on a rolling short-term basis.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>This site sets no cookies and runs no advertising trackers.</strong>
          There is no script that identifies you, no advertising pixel, and no
          cross-site profiling. That is also why there is no cookie consent banner —
          there is nothing to consent to.
        </p>
        <p>
          Fonts are self-hosted and served from bramlabs.co. Loading a page here does
          not make a request to Google Fonts or any other third-party font CDN.
        </p>

        <h2>What is never done</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Personal information is not sold, and never has been.</li>
          <li>
            Your email address is not added to a mailing list, used as an
            advertising audience, or shared with data brokers.
          </li>
          <li>No account is required to browse this site or read any policy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who else processes data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts and serves bramlabs.co, and
            processes standard request logs.
            <a
              href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Their privacy policy ↗</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Resend</strong> — delivers email sent through the forms on this
            site to the BramLabs inbox.
            <a
              href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Their privacy policy ↗</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Product-specific policies</h2>
        <p>
          Each published product has its own policy describing what that product
          does on your device or in your browser:
        </p>
        <ul>
          {
            products.map((p) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`/software/${p.slug}/privacy/`}>{p.title}</a> — {p.platform}
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live you may have the right to access the personal
          data held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict or
          object to processing, and to receive it in a portable format. In the UK
          and EEA these rights come from the GDPR; in California, from the
          CCPA/CPRA, which also protects you from being treated differently for
          exercising them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:contact@bramlabs.co">contact@bramlabs.co</a> to
          exercise any of them. Requests are answered within 30 days, at no charge.
          Since no personal information is sold, there is nothing to opt out of
          under "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information."
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13 and BramLabs does not
          knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child
          has sent personal information through a form here, email
          <a href="mailto:contact@bramlabs.co">contact@bramlabs.co</a> and it will
          be deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          Traffic is served over TLS. To report a vulnerability, see the
          <a href="/security/">security page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Material changes update the effective date at the top of this page. The
          current version took effect on {effective}.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          BramLabs — <a href="mailto:contact@bramlabs.co">contact@bramlabs.co</a>
          <br />
          Product support — <a href="mailto:support@bramlabs.co">support@bramlabs.co</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .effective {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }

  .summary {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ink);
    padding-left: var(--s-3);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
